WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
In this video you see how email keeps you informed when you are away from the site. The app is real; the server is a local stand-in, and the people and events are made up.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:26.000
When you RSVP to an event, a confirmation goes to your inbox, with the calendar file attached. Emails are queued with the action itself, then sent within minutes and retried if the mail service is busy.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:36.000
In Settings, the Email me when card shows what you get by email. Event changes, invites, role changes and the like always reach you.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Announcements are the one thing you can switch off. Turn off Email me announcements and the choice is saved straight away.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Turning announcements off does not silence anything else. Cancellations, confirmations and invites still reach you, and every link in an email is secure.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.000
That is email: reliable, with a plain-text copy, and under your control where it counts.

